ices","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The Kerberos realm, requested principals, node2 keytab, and end-to-end analyst service-ticket workflow are directly demonstrated and survived serial restarts. Both restart protocols include healthy pre-state, acknowledgement and disruption, changed boot identity, recovered state, and successful post-restart Kerberos behavior; fixed lifecycle boot observations independently agree. Platform preservation and native-package compatibility are also demonstrated. The only task-outcome gap is the lack of a final integrity observation for the node1 copy of the seeded ownership notes.","limitations":["No after-executor command or lifecycle probe inspected /srv/legacy2/kerberos-service-identity on node1, so that copy's preservation cannot be verified.","The retained SSH authorization/private key conclusion follows from the complete command timeline having no cleanup action; lifecycle snapshots did not inventory those root-owned files."]}
